target: internal/plan/plan.go
verify: go test ./internal/plan/ -count=1 -run 'TestAFailedAuthProbeSaysWhatItSaw'
expect: --- FAIL: TestAFailedAuthProbeSaysWhatItSaw/the_sandbox_keyring_failure
why:    `gh auth status` prints the host first and the failure on an `X` line under it — measured in the sandbox, gh 2.102.0: "github.com" then "  X Failed to log in to github.com account narthur (keyring)". Taking the first line makes the reason "gh auth status failed (github.com)", which names a host and no failure, so the operator learns nothing the skip did not already say.
